 gives \n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=\\frac{5}{2x}W(x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343264/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "357839bc-6cf7-532d-a4cd-ce4b64aefc41"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343264"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343256/field-1/8068f1a5e1ff3ce09232f84a5e253c47fe2c1b9f323ea9143f75c04509671e5a" :answer/id #uuid "2abcf027-e933-519a-94d9-043a1fa284a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343256/field-1/06eb5473a416ddf56821e165239df3cdfb6b9767260aa3432f26dca9b6281ad0" :answer/id #uuid "7c865006-2c69-526a-941d-108b75e72e3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343256/field-1/541e31cdc807fef7a519e5e501db8c2514e965bd94437e666f886a9a3d1975fc" :answer/id #uuid "dd7fa634-3581-541f-8e7a-ca6b0b174c56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343256/field-1/3942bb398cc99944722034999498371e518b1d75cc1c9f0fee14c17258e3d379" :answer/id #uuid "c2ddf590-365e-59a1-8ece-dce00aa27200" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{x}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343256/field-1/0ccd255554197a93c5e9567ee0c6aba33e0fe0a0c0a68a990aba6b38aacec915" :answer/id #uuid "40d9e584-68ce-5ae7-b4bc-105dfd87aa5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343256/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6ffd9db-eaaf-5f89-96f5-487b82c86206" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-343256/field-1/3942bb398cc99944722034999498371e518b1d75cc1c9f0fee14c17258e3d379" :answer-field/choices ["q-343256/field-1/8068f1a5e1ff3ce09232f84a5e253c47fe2c1b9f323ea9143f75c04509671e5a" "q-343256/field-1/06eb5473a416ddf56821e165239df3cdfb6b9767260aa3432f26dca9b6281ad0" "q-343256/field-1/541e31cdc807fef7a519e5e501db8c2514e965bd94437e666f886a9a3d1975fc" "q-343256/field-1/3942bb398cc99944722034999498371e518b1d75cc1c9f0fee14c17258e3d379" "q-343256/field-1/0ccd255554197a93c5e9567ee0c6aba33e0fe0a0c0a68a990aba6b38aacec915"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343256" :question/id #uuid "14454f59-3ca6-50f2-ab4a-60ef1b368cb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-343256" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+{e}^{x}{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the second-order homogeneous differential equation above. Let ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions, and let $W(x)$ be their Wronskian. Which differential equation must $W(x)$ satisfy?$\\,$\n${W}^{′}(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into Abel's identity gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′}(x) & =-{e}^{x}W(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343256/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "357839bc-6cf7-532d-a4cd-ce4b64aefc41"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343256"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186216625 :answer-field/correct 17592186216626 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-342709"] :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the second-order homogeneous differential equation above. Let ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions, and let $W(x)$ be their Wronskian. Which differential equation must $W(x)$ satisfy?$\\,$\n${W}^{′}(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=-{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into Abel's identity gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′}(x) & ={x}^{2}W(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-343266/field-1/1ab602dc52b1b72c8416ae99d6b81f1039b58837dcdeecadabdc9cf4851b0503" :answer/id #uuid "6612a5c3-7365-59e4-af2c-8d05df31e370" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{x}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343266/field-1/e022f14f95f76df3cfbdc01757d90e03d4e6508161a26d5787968927e21997a9" :answer/id #uuid "9fa7a9c7-af21-5be2-b29a-6810063b7d09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343266/field-1/3cca05f0e66f0cc9335900b36062d119f336433b58978fd63f89fdc8f4714efc" :answer/id #uuid "25ac9f3b-47df-582a-8bc0-156ef48bcc1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343266/field-1/3942bb398cc99944722034999498371e518b1d75cc1c9f0fee14c17258e3d379" :answer/id #uuid "00a0f95c-4557-5998-ab23-7ab0fe9a534a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{x}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343266/field-1/b34f03b80c15983bbf99fbbcc004f613c5907ec5c7e015e90afd96fd0aa52e18" :answer/id #uuid "067e7f21-cf9b-5eb2-9f75-690b906e1f32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+1}W(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343266/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b5bd86f-1d21-509e-b9a3-bfc3fb18d87c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-343266/field-1/3cca05f0e66f0cc9335900b36062d119f336433b58978fd63f89fdc8f4714efc" :answer-field/choices ["q-343266/field-1/1ab602dc52b1b72c8416ae99d6b81f1039b58837dcdeecadabdc9cf4851b0503" "q-343266/field-1/e022f14f95f76df3cfbdc01757d90e03d4e6508161a26d5787968927e21997a9" "q-343266/field-1/3cca05f0e66f0cc9335900b36062d119f336433b58978fd63f89fdc8f4714efc" "q-343266/field-1/3942bb398cc99944722034999498371e518b1d75cc1c9f0fee14c17258e3d379" "q-343266/field-1/b34f03b80c15983bbf99fbbcc004f613c5907ec5c7e015e90afd96fd0aa52e18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343266" :question/id #uuid "dbe79ebb-dced-566b-a58c-a1fb18f2d4a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-343266" :question/problem "$$\n({x}^{2}+1){y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=0,\\,x>0\n$$\n\nConsider the second-order homogeneous differential equation above. Let ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions, and let $W(x)$ be their Wronskian. Which differential equation must $W(x)$ satisfy?$\\,$\n${W}^{′}(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in standard form. Since $x>0$, we can divide both sides by ${x}^{2}+1$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}{y}^{′}+\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{2}+1}y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into Abel's identity gives \n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}W(x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343266/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "357839bc-6cf7-532d-a4cd-ce4b64aefc41"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343266"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343281/field-1/055d94d6d052153bc44ba9ead0a8abb3f1419ff7f0a6f422905fd686294ae920" :answer/id #uuid "fd278087-ca94-5b5a-ac16-e490b0c9f661" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343281/field-1/0a370ab19c6fe6213f75b34f79d516e7197c619afb62c6d14dac85afe6020dbd" :answer/id #uuid "8323690f-a235-505e-9a7b-65108d52eb7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343281/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4df341e2-332a-5514-8bfd-57b58df35612" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343281/field-1/055d94d6d052153bc44ba9ead0a8abb3f1419ff7f0a6f422905fd686294ae920" :answer-field/choices ["q-343281/field-1/055d94d6d052153bc44ba9ead0a8abb3f1419ff7f0a6f422905fd686294ae920" "q-343281/field-1/0a370ab19c6fe6213f75b34f79d516e7197c619afb62c6d14dac85afe6020dbd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343281" :question/id #uuid "810dae74-735d-536c-8276-1e6046370c4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-343281" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-3{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+(1+x)y=0.\n$$\n\nSuppose ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions and their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies $W(1)=1.$ What is $W(2)?$\n\n$W(2)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=-3{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=3{x}^{2}W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =3{x}^{2}W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =3{x}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & ={x}^{3}+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{{x}^{3}} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(1) & =C{e}^{{1}^{3}} \\\\ 1 & =Ce \\\\ C & ={e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\nW(x)={e}^{-1}{e}^{{x}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $W(2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(2) & ={e}^{-1}{e}^{{2}^{3}}={e}^{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343281/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84813773-2fbc-5752-8f31-8e547c9f79e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343281"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343280/field-1/bc3b03e004d34b93d9775158db235c043ca49c437950d01f9c260ce565d55b66" :answer/id #uuid "acb9656d-f714-5f54-a52f-ef80e320cf40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5e^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343280/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9bfc10f5-38bc-5d63-a026-9211b3baaeb0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343280/field-1/bc3b03e004d34b93d9775158db235c043ca49c437950d01f9c260ce565d55b66" :answer-field/choices ["q-343280/field-1/bc3b03e004d34b93d9775158db235c043ca49c437950d01f9c260ce565d55b66"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343280" :question/id #uuid "bbcbc989-2062-54fc-9c57-039f60296a1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-343280" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){y}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nSuppose ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions and their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies $W(0)=5.$ What is $W(\\pi )?$\n\n$W(\\pi )=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(0)=5$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(0) & =C{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)} \\\\ 5 & =C{e}^{1} \\\\ C & =5{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\nW(x)=5{e}^{-1}{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $W(\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(\\pi ) & =5{e}^{-1}{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )}=5{e}^{-1}{e}^{-1}=5{e}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343280/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84813773-2fbc-5752-8f31-8e547c9f79e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343280"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343268/field-1/80be74dd3655fc061aa59382e93baef1436a20b0813d3492b166b5e4258519f8" :answer/id #uuid "d7f45fa4-5367-5e70-bf7e-45601e93674b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5e^{-6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343268/field-1/24db6e4d8143cc434e0d88058309afb0d16fd01e69f698578d637591e1774d77" :answer/id #uuid "c0fc3e51-7cae-577b-a0be-4881a008d40d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5e^{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343268/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc3c9419-2dbe-5d02-a130-29d3fba4f698" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343268/field-1/80be74dd3655fc061aa59382e93baef1436a20b0813d3492b166b5e4258519f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-343268/field-1/80be74dd3655fc061aa59382e93baef1436a20b0813d3492b166b5e4258519f8" "q-343268/field-1/24db6e4d8143cc434e0d88058309afb0d16fd01e69f698578d637591e1774d77"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343268" :question/id #uuid "7d3b6731-589f-5445-b353-7fd925ffc6cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-343268" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}-7y=0.\n$$\n\nSuppose ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions and their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies $W(0)=5.$ What is $W(3)?$\n\n$W(3)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-2W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-2W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-2\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-2x+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{-2x} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(0)=5$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(0) & =C{e}^{-2\\cdot 0} \\\\ 5 & =C \\\\ C & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\nW(x)=5{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $W(3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(3) & =5{e}^{-2\\cdot 3}=5{e}^{-6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343268/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84813773-2fbc-5752-8f31-8e547c9f79e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343268"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343279/field-1/ee03e764da533b216d0b15926d35f6c9f5206b11c9706423c15987488f058a26" :answer/id #uuid "8c7841cf-390f-57cb-a1d3-0168dd073520" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343279/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc92c137-b1f6-5798-ae2c-aa397ad863fe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343279/field-1/ee03e764da533b216d0b15926d35f6c9f5206b11c9706423c15987488f058a26" :answer-field/choices ["q-343279/field-1/ee03e764da533b216d0b15926d35f6c9f5206b11c9706423c15987488f058a26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343279" :question/id #uuid "eaa3d462-e129-5a72-b685-0d958f0b6d99" :question/math-academy-id "q-343279" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+(\\frac{2}{x}+1){y}^{′}+(2-x)y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSuppose ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions and their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies $W(1)=3.$ What is $W(2)?$\n\n$W(2)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{2}{x}+1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-(\\frac{2}{x}+1)W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-(\\frac{2}{x}+1)W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-(\\frac{2}{x}+1)\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -(\\frac{2}{x}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{x}^{-2}{e}^{-x} \\\\ W & =\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(1)=3$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(1) & =\\frac{C}{{1}^{2}}{e}^{-1} \\\\ 3 & =C{e}^{-1} \\\\ C & =3e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\nW(x)=\\frac{3e}{{x}^{2}}{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $W(2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(2) & =\\frac{3e}{{2}^{2}}{e}^{-2}=\\frac{3}{4e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343279/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84813773-2fbc-5752-8f31-8e547c9f79e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343279"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343272/field-1/4dc35abf14ed8c6e94385ead9077472a7e608c8164af2944b38d26a6a66b6866" :answer/id #uuid "1da73127-b557-53c9-b0d0-0c0221dccf63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e^{-10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343272/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "57bfb22c-a9e3-5466-8464-fbb1f2696d4f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343272/field-1/4dc35abf14ed8c6e94385ead9077472a7e608c8164af2944b38d26a6a66b6866" :answer-field/choices ["q-343272/field-1/4dc35abf14ed8c6e94385ead9077472a7e608c8164af2944b38d26a6a66b6866"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343272" :question/id #uuid "c192ea08-e893-5ee6-88c7-eabdc991e52d" :question/math-academy-id "q-343272" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nSuppose ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions and their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies $W(1)=2.$ What is $W(3)?$\n\n$W(3)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-5W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-5W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-5\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -5\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-5x+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{-5x} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{-5x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(1)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(1) & =C{e}^{-5\\cdot 1} \\\\ 2 & =C{e}^{-5} \\\\ C & =2{e}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\nW(x)=2{e}^{5}{e}^{-5x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $W(3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(3) & =2{e}^{5}{e}^{-5\\cdot 3}=2{e}^{-10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343272/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84813773-2fbc-5752-8f31-8e547c9f79e6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343272"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343293/field-1/412793739940b973be2b527fb17aec02d6ca6345201ec8cd477bb75bb5283b50" :answer/id #uuid "4f86af7a-77cc-50ad-9f2a-66595f1fa296" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343293/field-1/1da555046aacb6be0b865c782bbfbb18c5b151194d3a2c31d76f44ce4d77f1d9" :answer/id #uuid "b68518c0-a075-5714-b075-8a30c9ba0694" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{Q(x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343293/field-1/491275c6478870d050061faaeb575b78630afda48101fd389c18926d9618d6bc" :answer/id #uuid "478d0a82-1f12-56e0-a31e-f2010e30814a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2xQ(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343293/field-1/e819017e19dccac106b8bdd7a345917915a57ae6ae3646d73f366105b31b91f7" :answer/id #uuid "c9de8fff-e971-536e-826f-5b355371dbf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343293/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf765dee-c8b0-52bb-97f2-b7bd6534bbe2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-343293/field-1/412793739940b973be2b527fb17aec02d6ca6345201ec8cd477bb75bb5283b50" :answer-field/choices ["q-343293/field-1/412793739940b973be2b527fb17aec02d6ca6345201ec8cd477bb75bb5283b50" "q-343293/field-1/1da555046aacb6be0b865c782bbfbb18c5b151194d3a2c31d76f44ce4d77f1d9" "q-343293/field-1/491275c6478870d050061faaeb575b78630afda48101fd389c18926d9618d6bc" "q-343293/field-1/e819017e19dccac106b8bdd7a345917915a57ae6ae3646d73f366105b31b91f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343293/field-2/fd52c5cb8d7be5045b3f482654d126d99a7a07c81cef773d1c58fac0419eed6a" :answer/id #uuid "c2025972-7109-505a-9272-c1a15b381210" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "C{e}^{-