37ff1cfe2285f70b07eaedfdf36fc578c9e108" :answer/id #uuid "63d0b04c-74a9-559d-b3f7-e71c3c5ffe22" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$W(x)\\ne 0$ for all $x>0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343293/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b7207e9-2b8a-543e-8b6c-5ae4aaff6051" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-343293/field-3/def9e284c04ff88f4501b741fdfd679144aa2f6e42b9c1ec7d4a2217819cc46c" :answer-field/choices ["q-343293/field-3/def9e284c04ff88f4501b741fdfd679144aa2f6e42b9c1ec7d4a2217819cc46c" "q-343293/field-3/4ddf0edc896c1f1ae6c38e2226560fa57e92098045c3c07394f525b12ebbd5f4" "q-343293/field-3/a8a92ea07ac7485e9fd6d2e4cc37ff1cfe2285f70b07eaedfdf36fc578c9e108"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343293" :question/id #uuid "4acb3708-3f85-57a1-975e-b6f23d95dbae" :question/math-academy-id "q-343293" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\\,x>0\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions to the second-order homogeneous differential equation above, where $Q(x)$ is continuous on $(0,\\infty ).$ The Wronskian satisfies $W(2)=0.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\nThe Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies the following first-order differential equation:\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)={{field-1}}W(x)\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we get\n\n$$\nW={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nNow, using the fact that $W(2)=0,$ we obtain \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=2x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-2xW(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-2xW \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-2x\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-{x}^{2}+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{-{x}^{2}} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(2)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(2) & =C{e}^{-{2}^{2}} \\\\ 0 & =C{e}^{-4} \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $W(x)=0\\text{ for all }x>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343293/field-1" "q-343293/field-2" "q-343293/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "734fe467-57d6-5b3f-a61e-1e2e4624b5fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343293"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343294/field-1/01966c973e10d8784d59569f76ee6a733cf6c09539de1f45ca700e5449a376ac" :answer/id #uuid "139c2d00-5609-5fee-8109-53cda1a34cb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{Q(x)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343294/field-1/6e07b0b713ed28c695c04a5d2c592ae82c16d7cade711336b5cc007480e64223" :answer/id #uuid "b8702eb2-7b5d-5b6b-9212-8b813cec1b91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-Q(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343294/field-1/0c938e2a9d59ed135c294c5e355997fe0f215407bbccca774b34eee5de4ffe21" :answer/id #uuid "4e0c68fa-6c7c-58ca-ae8f-a0599b8846ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343294/field-1/e9fc4399b90dface734b25c382d3284f47f36862134bc2e78b1bc90304839f43" :answer/id #uuid "0077df0a-c9c5-5cb1-a77c-9304a2a65a35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343294/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "094c8c4f-9c46-5a96-9f9a-9b2971fc0c91" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-343294/field-1/e9fc4399b90dface734b25c382d3284f47f36862134bc2e78b1bc90304839f43" :a